course: dictionary
lesson: 6388
title: Multiply: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word multiply has two meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. In maths, to multiply is to add the same number many times in one quick step. «Count each kind of coin, multiply by its value, and add all the amounts.» Here multiply means finding the total of equal groups.
explain: The other meaning is to grow quickly in number. «Antibiotics kill bacteria or stop them multiplying» means stop germs from growing in number. Clues like «times», «groups of», «rows of» and «each» point to maths, while words like rabbits, germs or living things point to growing.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «3 multiplied by 4 is 12»: adding 3 four times gives 12, so the maths meaning fits. If you read «Rabbits multiply fast» and put in the maths meaning, it does not make sense, so the growing meaning is right.
fact: Multiply means to add the same number many times in one quick step. Its sign is ×.
fact: «3 multiplied by 4 is 12» because 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 = 12.
fact: Multiply can also mean to grow quickly in number: «Links multiply fast».
fact: Clue words such as «times», «groups of», «rows of», «each» and «packs of» often point to multiplying.
fact: In science, living things multiply, which means they have many young, and germs multiply in warm places.
exercise: «Count each kind of coin, multiply by its value, and add all the amounts.» In this sentence, multiply means | *Add the same number many times | Take one away from the total | Lose count of the coins
exercise: What is 4 multiplied by 3? | *12 | 34 | 1 | 7
exercise: Which word is a clue that a sum is about multiplying? | *Groups of | Yesterday | Hungry | Quiet
test: «Rabbits multiply fast.» What does multiply mean here? | To wash | To take away | *To grow quickly in number | To sing loudly
test: «Adding the same amount in a loop is multiplying (5 turns of +3 is 15).» How much is 5 turns of +3? | 8 | 3 | *15 | 53
exam: «Germs multiply in warm places.» Which meaning fits best? | Add the same number many times in one step | *Grow quickly in number | Sing loudly | Cool down quickly
